 The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 
+## Local network access
+
+Open **Local network** in the footer to fetch an HTTP(S) resource from a LAN
+device or a loopback service (`localhost`, `127.0.0.1`, or `[::1]`). Select the
+resource location, enter its URL, and select **Connect**. Requests run in the
+user's browser, never through the application server, and only after submitting
+the form. Responses are displayed as plain text.
+
+Deploy the application over HTTPS. The browser may ask for Local network or
+Loopback network permission; blocked permissions must be changed in site
+settings. Unsupported Permissions API queries fall back to a user-initiated
+request under the browser's normal networking rules; browser support for HTTP
+local resources varies. The target service must allow the application's origin
+with standard CORS headers. The middleware explicitly permits `local-network`
+and `loopback-network` for this origin only. Requests declare `targetAddressSpace`
+so supporting browsers can handle HTTP local resources from HTTPS pages.
+
 ## Tech Stack
 
 - **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
